<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banu Makhzum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banu Makhzum was a wealthy clan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quraysh">Quraysh</a> tribe of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, prominent in trade and warfare before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Its leader Abu Jahl was among Muhammad's fiercest opponents, while the clan also produced the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a>, who later led the early Muslim conquests.</p></div>
